{title: Here We Come A-Wassailing}

{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[C]Here we come a-wassailing,
among the leaves so green,
[F]Here we come a [C]wand'ring,
so [G]fair to be seen.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus"}

Love and [C]joy [F]come to [C]you,
And to you your [F]wassail [C]too,
And God [C]bless you and [G]send you a [Am]happy new [F]year,
And God [C]send you a [G]happy new [C]year.

{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[C]Wé are nót dailý beggárs,
that beg from door to door,
[F]But we are neigh-bor’s [C]children,
whom [G]you have seen before.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

[C]Good master and good mistress,
As you sit beside the fire,
Pray [F]think of us poor [C]children,
Who [G]wander in the mire.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}

[C]Call up the butler of the house,
put on his golden ring,
[F]Let him bring us all a [C]glass of beer,
and [G]better we shall sing.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Repeat Chorus}
